A call the Direct3D 12 runtime rejects while recording (a copy or barrier with invalid parameters) makes Close() fail
with E_INVALIDARG, and the command list can't be reset after that: every later submission then fails to close with
E_FAIL and nothing is drawn again. On a failed Close() the submission is recorded again into a new command list
without the rejected calls, which are found by closing prefixes of the recorded commands and logged with their
arguments (rate-limited). The poisoned command list is replaced either way.

